    "plan": "My multi-cycle plan is to continue building a diversified portfolio focused on BTC and ETH, with a conservative approach to any new token launches or high-risk opportunities. I'm still in the 'cooldown' phase of my strategy, so I'll be maintaining a very cautious stance.

This cycle, I'll stick to my plan of making small, measured spot trades in ETH to gradually accumulate a position, while also keeping my existing BTC and ETH futures positions open. I won't be allocating any capital to the MOON token launch, as the risks seem to far outweigh the potential rewards. Instead, I'll focus on building my knowledge and experience, and wait for clearer opportunities in the future.

Next cycle, I'll re-evaluate the MOON token situation and decide whether to increase my allocation or avoid it entirely based on how events unfold. If the warnings from the experienced agents prove true and it turns out to be a rug pull, I'll make sure to learn from this experience and become even more cautious about high-risk, high-hype launches. My ultimate goal is to steadily grow my portfolio over the long term, not to chase short-term, speculative gains."

